WEBVTT

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.050
1958.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.720
Akagi Shigeru, the genius who 
suddenly descended into the darkness.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.530
He was just 13 when he emerged victorious

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.640
from the death match against the 
Kawada group's rep player, Ichikawa.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.190
After that, he vanished without a trace.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:26.190
Six years have passed since then.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.360
1964.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.710
All of Japan was excited 
about the Tokyo Olympics.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.680
Are you certain, Yasuoka-san?

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.020
Lying wouldn't get me anywhere.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.360
People who know him would 
know it when they see him.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.740
Then it's really

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.090
<b>Kawada Group Boss
Kawada</b>

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.090
the one from that legendary night?

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:06.100
Yes, these last six years, 
nobody knew where he was.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.110
It is the Akagi Shigeru.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:18.110
You will be able to witness another 
legendary tale of the undefeatable man...

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.610
Delivered by Akagi Shigeru.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.980
Ishikawa.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.850
<b>Kawada Group Underboss
Ishikawa</b>

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:22.850
Yes.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.860
You're the only one in our group 
who has seen Akagi play in person.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.940
I'll leave this to you.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:31.870
Yes.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.710
I've brought him.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.730
Come in.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:45.760
This is Akagi Shigeru.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.460
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.460
<b>The Sign of Rebirth</b>

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.910
Let's see how you play.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.640
We've supplied additional players.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.690
That's all right, isn't it, Yasuoka-san?

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.820
That's fine.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.560
<i>That godly play I saw six years ago 
isn't something that anyone can do.</i>

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.840
<i>If that sort of play is recreated right here,</i>

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.220
<i>I'll have no choice but to believe</i>

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.100
<i>that the Akagi Shigeru here is the real deal.</i>

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.760
<i>The perfect tile to draw.</i>

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.580
<i>He can now go from a double 
pon wait to a two-sided wait.</i>

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:36.850
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.360
<i>He kept the double pon wait?</i>

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:44.100
<i>Why did he stick with that if 
it won't give him a pinfu?</i>

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.190
Tsumo!

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.710
<i>What's with his luck?</i>

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.350
<b>Daisangen</b>

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.350
It was a ridiculous draw.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:12.860
But after this, Akagi kept making 
impossible draws and wins.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.590
And in the last hand...

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.370
<i>He's got a junchan hand.</i>

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.850
<i>He has to discard the 6 of circles.</i>

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.810
Riichi.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.380
<i>Again!</i>

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.410
<i>He did something inexplicable again.</i>

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.940
Ippatsu tsumo.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.130
Riichi, pinfu, sanshoku.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:45.890
Haneman.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.950
Looks like Akagi dominated 
these two East-South matches.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.740
I don't get how he can continue 
to get all these crazy draws.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.530
It's simple.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.200
Simple?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.750
Akagi, do it.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.450
Akagi gathers 17 tiles, looks at them 
for an instant, and puts them down.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.000
He repeats this 8 times.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:45.310
In other words, 17 x 8 tiles, 
136 tiles, are now facedown.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.310
Ishikawa-san, it doesn't matter 
which, just name any hand.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.320
Akagi will put together that hand 
while the tiles are facedown.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.320
He'll pick the tiles facedown?

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.990
Yes, he's memorized all of the 136 tiles here.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.460
That's ridiculous! Memorized?

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:07.630
He didn't have time for that. 
He only glanced at them.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:11.360
That's all he needs. 
Please, name a hand.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.640
Then, a sanshoku.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.100
Okay, next, a kokushi musou.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.610
Daisangen tsuuiisou!

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.610
Tsuuiisou - A hand composed exclusively of wind and dragon tiles.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.890
<i>After a kokushi musou, 
this should be difficult.</i>

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.380
<i>He won't be able to make it unless he 
knows the position of every honor tile.</i>

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.130
<i>That is indeed amazing.</i>

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:15.870
<i>His memorization skill could be called godly.</i>

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.880
<i>But something's off.</i>

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.320
<i>I can't shake that feeling.</i>

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:25.090
<i>What was amazing about Akagi 
Shigeru was not something like that.</i>

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:34.590
<i>What I saw six years ago was something 
totally different, something mysterious.</i>

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:38.800
<i>It was something far beyond
the scope of normal people like us.</i>

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:49.870
So?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:52.320
Akagi has become weaker.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.440
It seems that his peak was six years ago,

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.870
and in a sense, he's not the same person.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:02.860
Nevertheless, he has abilities that 
far surpass those of normal people.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.520
Then I don't care.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.460
No matter how much he has weakened,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.620
it's irrelevant as long as there 
is nobody who can beat him.

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:19.340
<i>I hate this.</i>

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.630
<i>I didn't want to see a second-rate Akagi.</i>

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.240
You bastard!

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.900
Think we're playing around?!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.140
Don't screw with us!

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.770
Come on, bitch!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.160
Are you shitting yourself?

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.140
The fuck are you looking at?

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.640
Four on one, huh?

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.640
Asshole!

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.750
H-Hey!

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.460
Damn you!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.990
I won't forget this!

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.370
Akagi Shigeru?

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:10.190
No, he has a completely different 
aura than the guy from before.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.880
It's like he's a different person.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:14.380
Are there two Akagi Shigerus?

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.810
Are you Akagi?

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.390
Are you Akagi Shigeru?

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:33.030
Are you the Akagi Shigeru who had a 
death match against the blind master,

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.130
Ichikawa, six years ago?

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.370
I don't expect you to remember who I am.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:43.150
After that match, you suddenly disappeared.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:45.170
We looked all over for you.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.420
H-Hey.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.420
Please wait!

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:02.400
Akagi?

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:03.520
Yes.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:09.770
It's been six years, so I realize 
he might be difficult to recognize.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.010
But Akagi is different.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.770
He was so unique and intense.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:20.090
So if Yasuoka-san is saying 
that that man is Akagi...

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.780
No, that man is someone else.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:23.900
Huh?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:27.880
It was just one night, but I have 
seen Akagi with my own eyes.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.640
That man is a fake.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.180
Yasuoka-san is just using Akagi's name.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.790
I'm sure about that.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:42.200
I came here today to ask for 
your help with the other Akagi.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.800
The other Akagi?

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:44.920
Yes.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.890
The man I met after seeing the fake Akagi

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:55.500
is the one who matched 
the Akagi of my memory.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:01.490
I asked my underlings and, 
apparently, he's quite notorious

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.850
among the local punks 
for picking random fights.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:05.890
Random fights?

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.860
Amateurs, yakuza members...
he'll pick a fight with anyone.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.860
It's like he knows no fear.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.770
It goes without saying that he's skilled.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.840
If you're with less than five people,

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.310
it's safest to avoid eye contact with him.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.370
You're saying that man is Akagi?

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.880
That's what I'd like you to confirm.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:29.380
We've already figured out where he is.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:31.850
A toy factory?

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:36.880
Akagi is a worker at this factory.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:40.270
Could you take a look through that gap?

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.520
He should be working right now.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:56.000
Well?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.860
That looks like him.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:01.010
So much, I could almost swear it's him.

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.510
Right?

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:07.510
But I can't believe that 
Akagi is doing honest work...

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.760
I'll hand out this month's pay now.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:25.820
Ishida-kun.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.990
Yes.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:27.890
Nagasawa-kun.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:28.830
Yes.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:29.770
Kawashima-kun.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.460
Yes.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:31.040
Furuya-kun.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:31.480
Yes.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.300
Tawara-kun.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:32.760
Yes.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:33.520
Nakatani-kun.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.770
Yes.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.770
Twelve thousand yen.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:40.690
In 1964, college graduates made 
about 20,000 yen at their first job.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.970
Hey, newcomer.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:48.410
It's our tradition to play 
Mahjong on our pay day here.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.790
You know how to play, right?

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.150
Sorry, but I don't feel like it today.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.600
Come on, don't be like that.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.560
It's also your welcoming party.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.670
We can't do that without you, can we?

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:06.240
Don't worry, we won't take all of your pay.

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:08.410
We'll leave you enough to eat.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.810
It's completely normal to pay 
a tuition in the beginning.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.910
It comes with being a member of society.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.420
So you'll basically be taking my money.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.550
Not necessarily.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.660
You could win, too.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.080
I suppose.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.530
You're right.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.870
Akagi-kun, you have a visitor.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:34.060
Akagi.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.030
Well, well...

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.770
There's no doubt,

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.920
you're the real Akagi.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:44.040
What's up, Nangou-san?

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.040
Do you have a minute?

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:47.910
Sure.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.550
Well, Senpai, you heard him.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:51.990
Is that okay?

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.100
It's not like I had plans.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.590
Osamu!

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.010
It'll have to be you again this month.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:03.020
But I did it last month, 
and the month before that...

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.970
Akagi says he won't do it, 
so you don't have a choice!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.700
If you want to blame someone, blame him.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.700
Akagi-san, please play instead of me.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.780
I'm going out now.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.380
If you don't want to play, just don't.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:20.540
It doesn't work that way...

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.930
We don't have enough players!

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:23.680
See?

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:26.220
Why don't you go to a Mahjong parlor?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.460
There will be plenty of players there,

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:33.220
and you'll be able to 
gamble all you want there.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:37.960
It's not like you really have to 
squeeze us for our cheap salary.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.460
You're gonna talk back to your senpai?!

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.190
Violence is not the solution!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.690
I'll remember this.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.460
For some reason, there are 
always two or three of those

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.680
ganging up at every workplace.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.220
I wonder why.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:00.210
Huh?

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:04.220
Why don't they live more rewarding lives?

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.630
I see what's up.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.330
I'm sorry, he said he just wanted to talk.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.030
Akagi, why are you 
wasting your time here?

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.030
You can't play around forever.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:23.390
You can't buy a life with the pocket change 
you get from working a normal job.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:30.660
Last week, the night I ran into you,

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.670
Yasuoka brought a fake Akagi over.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.380
He's just as crooked as always, that cop.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:42.030
So does this fake look like me?

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:46.390
Of course he looks like you, 
but he actually plays well, too.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:51.400
He is assuming your identity. 
He couldn't do that if he was a loser.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:57.310
There were two matches this week 
where he played as our rep player.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:58.900
He made it through both without a hitch.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:00.410
<i>Tsumo.</i>

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.100
He didn't win an astonishing amount,

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.910
but his play style was stable 
from beginning to end.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:13.950
Our boss seems to like his clever 
play style and trusts him quite a lot.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.920
But I'm worried.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.280
Worried?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:24.890
It's true that he has skill, 
but it's still within the human realm.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.350
If we tried hard enough, 
we could probably match him.

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:32.170
As a gambler, he's second-rate.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.550
Second-rate...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.410
He's the type that will never be 
able to play on a godly level.

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:39.970
He'll lose eventually.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:43.370
When he encounters the real villains

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:46.550
and the demons of this world, 
he'll be torn to shreds.

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.150
Green.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:57.260
The only one who can fight 
those villains is you, Akagi.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:17:00.540
I'm just going to take a look at the fake.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.870
I don't want anything else to do with this.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.730
Yeah, that's right.

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:11.550
I see, you found the real one.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.240
Good work.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.010
However, I don't need him any longer.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:17.510
What?

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:21.540
Ishikawa, I have a high opinion of that man.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.880
The one you call the fake.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.890
He's a new kind of rep player.

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.700
Every single move he makes is ruled by logic.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.530
He never plays by gut instinct.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:38.300
He has the sensibility and 
readiness to prioritize actual facts

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.320
as well as keen eyes to spot these.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.170
He doesn't win big, but he 
doesn't lose big, either.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:45.510
His wins have a stability to them.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:50.010
We don't need godly skill in our rep players.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:53.110
What's important is the average.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:56.850
Don't you agree, Ishikawa?

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.140
Yes...

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.850
Excuse me.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:03.950
Yasuoka-san!

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:11.570
<i>So that's the other Akagi.</i>

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:18.610
<i>He does look like him.</i>

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.580
Ishikawa, I'll show you something fun.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:31.320
I wonder if the real one can do it, too.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.590
Yasuoka-kun, please have him do that thing.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:35.340
Yes, sir.

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:41.330
After being instructed by Yasuoka,

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.930
the fake Akagi first turns 
all 136 tiles facedown.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:49.700
Then he randomly picks 
13 tiles and opens them.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:50.700
Three.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:58.210
Then he picks another 
13 tiles and opens them.

00:18:58.210 --> 00:18:59.210
Two.

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:02.180
Boss, what is he doing?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.860
It's the shanten number.

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:04.580
Shanten?

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:08.180
The shanten number is the number of 
tiles a hand needs to get into tenpai.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:12.320
A hand that requires three tiles to be 
in tenpai is called a three shanten hand.

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:17.060
He instantly finds the shanten 
number and says it out loud.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:18.380
<i>That's crazy.</i>

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:21.070
<i>He's doing it in a flash without 
even ordering the tiles.</i>

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:25.070
<i>The first one was three, 
and the second one was two...</i>

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.070
Hey, order the tiles.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:37.080
<i>The first one was a three 
shanten hand, and the next...</i>

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.160
<i>Two shanten.</i>

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:40.590
<i>No mistakes.</i>

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.090
<i>How can he do it so fast?</i>

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.090
Five.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:50.260
What the fake Akagi is doing here 
isn't amazing in and of itself.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:53.100
With enough time, anybody can do it.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:57.070
Except he does it five to ten times 
faster than normal people.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.290
It's an awe-inspiring speed.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.100
Four.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.770
<i>Ishikawa-san said he's second-rate,</i>

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:06.990
<i>but this man's a different 
kind of genius than Akagi.</i>

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:09.700
After this, the fake Akagi

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.180
kept repeating this superhuman 
feat without missing a beat.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:16.720
And just when he was about to 
uncover the last set of tiles

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:19.040
that he picked from the last 19...

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:21.630
Three.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:27.920
Three?

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.110
He hasn't even opened the hand yet!

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:34.550
How many?

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:35.610
What's the shanten number?

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.290
Uh...

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.110
Order them, order them!

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:44.280
<i>No sets of three...</i>

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.910
<i>And four sets of two, with one pair.</i>

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:48.520
<i>Which means...</i>

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.020
<i>Three shanten!</i>

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:54.020
<i>He got it right!</i>

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:02.000
The genius Akagi Shigeru has 
descended into the darkness again.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:05.680
This is the beginning of a new legend.

00:22:16.220 --> 00:22:19.090
Next time, "The Authenticity of Genius."

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:20.510
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:20.510
<b>The Authenticity of Genius</b>
